/// - `jj.detect_failed` — an I/O error (e.g. `EACCES`, `ENOTDIR`) prevented classification.
/// - `ffi.null_pointer` — `path` is a null pointer.
/// - `ffi.utf8_error` — `path` contains invalid UTF-8.
///
/// # Safety
/// `path` must be a valid, NUL-terminated C string or null. The returned `*mut ZanshinBuf`
/// is heap-allocated and must be freed exactly once via `zanshin_buffer_free_token`.
@ffi.Native<ffi.Pointer<ZanshinBuf> Function(ffi.Pointer<ffi.Char>)>()
external ffi.Pointer<ZanshinBuf> zanshin_repo_detect(
  ffi.Pointer<ffi.Char> path,
);

/// Create a new jj repository — the CLI's `jj git init` (Story 9.20), or a workspace on jj's
/// native backend.
///
/// The arguments cross as a `RepoInitRequest` `FlatBuffers` request buffer, one field per CLI
/// parameter: `path` (REQUIRED; created when missing, one level, for the Git backend), `backend`
/// (`Native` — Zanshin-only, the path must exist and no Git flag applies — or `Git`), `colocate` /
/// `no_colocate` (the CLI's two flags; neither = `git.colocate`), `object_hash` (`Unspecified` =
/// `git.object-hash`). Over an existing `.git/` a colocated init runs the CLI's External flow (the
/// steps `zanshin_repo_convert` runs; neither rolls back); `--no-colocate` there is refused.
